From: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: orangepi-zero: disable mmc0 (SD card unused at runtime)

The rootfs is an initramfs bundled into the kernel and usbproxy-trim.cfg
compiles out EXT4_FS/FAT_FS, so Linux never mounts anything from the SD card -
`mount | grep mmc` on a running appliance is empty. The controller was still
probing and staying clocked for the whole uptime: BUS_CLK_GATING_REG0
(0x01c20060) read 0x22800040 with bit 6 (mmc0) set, and the sunxi-mmc interrupt
ticked over at ~1/s on an otherwise idle board (measured 2026-08-06 with
scripts/power-probe.py).

U-Boot reads the card before the kernel starts and uses its own DTB, so this
does not affect booting. The only capability lost is poking the card from the
running system, which nothing does.

Applies on top of 0003 (appliance trim) and 0004 (CPU cap + ramoops), which
also touch this file - hence the separate patch with post-0004 line numbers.

Signed-off-by: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
@@ -179,7 +179,12 @@
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PF6 */
-	status = "okay";
+	/* SD card unused at runtime: the rootfs is an initramfs bundled into
+	 * the kernel and EXT4_FS/FAT_FS are compiled out, so nothing is ever
+	 * mounted from it. U-Boot reads the card (with its own DTB) before the
+	 * kernel starts, so boot is unaffected. Leaving it enabled kept the
+	 * controller clocked and ticking for the whole uptime. */
+	status = "disabled";
 };

 &mmc1 {
